WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.167
(gentle guitar music)

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.240
[Kim] Hey, Rob, this is Kim Katie

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.060
from Louisville, Kentucky.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.540
So today you wake up and you
decide to write a screenplay

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.360
set in Dayton, Ohio.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.210
Yes, that's right.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:18.230
What story would you tell

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.370
and who would you cast?

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.290
Name three people you
really want to work with

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:28.290
outside of yourself, and
that's my question for today.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:30.670
I've read all your books,

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.923
love your podcast, and
hope you have a great day.

00:00:34.923 --> 00:00:35.800
Thanks.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.600
Thank you, Kim, for calling in

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.450
and also thank you for reading the books.

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.553
Always like to hear that.

00:00:40.553 --> 00:00:42.350
Well, there's two things at play here.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.710
There's what I would
write about Dayton, Ohio,

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.600
and who I would cast,

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.750
and then who my three favorite people are.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.350
So I gotta figure out do
my three favorite people,

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.350
oh, actually!

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:56.040
I was worried about having my
three favorite people be able

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.920
to be in my Dayton, Ohio, story.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.300
So Joaquin Phoenix is, I
think, my favorite actor

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:07.460
at the moment, and I think
he's going to play Papine.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.210
Papine was the neighborhood
hood in Dayton, Ohio,

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:15.150
who may or may not have been
like, you know, convict.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.290
Yeah, he was like the rough,
he might've had a switchblade

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:23.250
and he would, you know, steal
things and he was the guy

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.300
we all kind of looked up to as a bad-ass.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.810
So maybe Joaquin Phoenix

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:31.810
in the Papine ding-dong-ditch
stealing, you know, you know,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.630
petty things out of the grocery store.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.437
And then eight-year-old Rob Lowe going,

00:01:38.437 --> 00:01:40.621
"Wow, I want to be like Papine."

00:01:40.621 --> 00:01:44.390
Unfortunately Papine
met his his untimely end

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.550
when he was being chased by the police

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:48.470
and jumped over a barbed wire fence

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:51.500
and the barbed wire
caught him in the nut sack

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.697
and he was rushed to the hospital

00:01:53.697 --> 00:01:55.563
and we never saw Papine again.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:00.100
That might prevent Joaquin
Phoenix from doing the role,

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.870
but that is the truth and
truth is, as you know,

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:03.970
stranger than fiction.

